# TASK-AI-155 — root-cause fix: one URL source of truth (39 rounds of the same class)

WHERE: apps/web/src/components/data-table/useDataTable.ts:116-200 (useSearchParams + popstate listener :125-130 + `historyEpoch` + `window.location.search` snapshot :137-138 + pending-navigation queue :150-175).
WRONG: two competing sources for table state (Next committed router params vs a pre-commit window.location snapshot and a hand-written queue). Reproduce: `/storybook?per_page=5` → Next → Back → Next: URL says page=2, table stays on page 1. Every round found a new variant of this desync (8 findings in this file).
GOAL (BR-UI-01): table state is a PURE function of the committed router params from `useSearchParams()` (or props.searchParams when server-provided). Delete the popstate listener, `historyEpoch`, the window.location snapshot and the pending queue. Table actions only call `router.replace/push` with the next params and never set local page/sort/filter state; the render follows the URL. Debounce only the filter text input (local draft text), not committed state. Keep the public hook API; if `historyEpoch` is in the returned type, remove it and update its callers.
VERIFY: tests in the existing useDataTable test file: (1) Next→Back→Next shows page 2 matching URL; (2) Back restores page 1 and rows; (3) rapid Next,Next yields page 3; (4) filter typing debounced then URL updated once. Run those tests, pnpm --filter web typecheck, pnpm lint, pnpm format:check, pnpm security:secrets. Size cap: net change should SHRINK the file.

## root-cause (extension, 07:45) — toolbar and faceted filter keep a second state machine

WHERE: apps/web/src/components/data-table/DataTableToolbar.tsx:103-118 (computeToolbarDraftOnPropChange), :271; DataTableFacetedFilter.tsx:246; useDataTable.ts:210-215 (getNextQueryBase) and the 2 remaining historyEpoch/window.location uses.
WRONG: "draft / acknowledgment / dispatch invalidation" machinery in the toolbar and facets re-creates the desync the hook fix removed; 6 new findings are all in it.
GOAL (BR-UI-01): the ONLY local state allowed is the search box's in-progress text, reset to the URL value whenever the committed URL value changes (one `useEffect` on that value). Facets have NO local state: checked = derived from URL params; a click calls the hook's setter which router.replace()s. getNextQueryBase builds from the current committed params only. Delete computeToolbarDraftOnPropChange, acknowledgment/invalidation logic and remaining historyEpoch/window.location code. Net line count of the three files must drop.
VERIFY: tests: typing then Back restores URL search text; facet toggle → URL updated and checkbox follows URL after Back/Forward; two quick facet clicks keep both values.

